WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.000
It took me forever but I figured out what
this newspaper says and what implications

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.529
it has for the story.

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:11.000
Stick around to the end of this video if you
want to see it.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.940
In 2017 I made one of the first movie Things
You Missed episodes on It: Chapter One.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.530
Here’s what I said at the end.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:24.550
“...and when the trailer for Chapter 2 drops
you can count on a Things You Missed episode

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:25.840
from me.”

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:30.270
And today that trailer did drop, so here’s
me keeping my promise, just as the Losers

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:35.120
Club keeps their promise to return to Derry,
should It rise again.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:38.329
The trailer begins with Beverly going back
to her father’s old apartment.

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:41.789
She hasn’t talked to him since moving to
Chicago years ago, and it would probably be

00:00:41.789 --> 00:00:45.559
a bit awkward, considering she smashed his
head open the last time they saw each other

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:46.970
in 1989.

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:50.480
When she arrives she discovers her father
is no longer there, instead there’s this

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.200
old woman named Mrs. Kersh.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.719
Beverly thinks that she may have misread the
name on the door, somehow confusing her own

00:00:55.719 --> 00:00:57.909
last name Marsh, with Kersh.

00:00:57.909 --> 00:01:01.219
But in the opening shot of the trailer it
clearly says: Marsh.

00:01:01.219 --> 00:01:06.000
Bev finds the postcard given to her by Ben
27 years ago while Mrs. Kersh is making tea,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.060
and if you pay attention to Beverly’s arms,
they are covered in bruises.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:13.500
In the novel, Bev has an abusive husband named
Tom, who she flees from to come to Derry.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.380
She also has something hanging around her
neck.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:18.940
I’m not sure what it is, but it reminds
me of the key she wore as a child.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:21.180
We never see what it’s for in the first
movie.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.720
Mrs. Kersh’s shirt is covered in birds,
and birds can be seen throughout her apartment,

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.340
which could be a clue about her true nature.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:30.470
It’s not really mentioned in Chapter 1,
but birds play a major part in the novel,

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:34.021
where Mike first encounters It in the form
of a giant bird that attacks him, and Stan

00:01:34.021 --> 00:01:38.070
would later use his vast knowledge of birds
to determine that It’s bird form is not

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.590
real, which weakens it.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:43.200
As Beverly looks around the apartment at the
photos, Mrs. Kersh peeks out and looks at

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:48.990
her, all naked and creepy like woman from
The Visit.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:53.460
The photo shows Pennywise in his human form,
Bob Grey, another detail that wasn’t a part

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.820
of the first film.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:57.950
Before she attacks, Mrs. Kersh asks the following
question:

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.410
“What about you?

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:04.010
Are you still his little girl Beverly?

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:06.480
Are you!?”

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.109
This is probably a reference to Beverly’s
fear of her father, and the fact that It takes

00:02:10.109 --> 00:02:14.019
the shape of her dad temporarily during the
final battle in Chapter 1.

00:02:14.019 --> 00:02:15.219
"Hey Bevvy.

00:02:15.219 --> 00:02:17.290
Are you still my little girl?

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:18.290
AGHHH!!"

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:21.519
Then we finally get our reveal shot of some
more members of the Losers Club including

00:02:21.519 --> 00:02:24.080
Mike, Richie, Bill, Beverly and Ben.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.210
Eddie doesn't show up until later in the trailer.

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:29.409
They see themselves as kids in the reflection
of this window, one of the many ways they

00:02:29.409 --> 00:02:32.989
become more childlike when they return to
Derry, much like how Bill gets his stutter

00:02:32.989 --> 00:02:37.219
back in the book, and the scars they cut into
their hands to make the promise reappear when

00:02:37.219 --> 00:02:38.349
they find out It’s back.

00:02:38.349 --> 00:02:40.659
They are also in front of an ice cream shop.

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:43.909
There is a scene where they get ice cream
in the book after Ben stands up for Beverly

00:02:43.909 --> 00:02:45.859
against this kid named Bradley Donovan.

00:02:45.859 --> 00:02:49.330
Hopefully the childhood flashbacks in It Chapter
2 are going to fill in some of the events

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:53.129
that took place that summer that they didn’t
have room for in the first movie, as opposed

00:02:53.129 --> 00:02:55.780
to the flashbacks just being used to reiterate
stuff.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:59.219
That looks to be the case because this shot
of them riding bikes is a completely different

00:02:59.219 --> 00:03:02.829
day than anything that happens in the first
one; I’ve never seen Richie wearing this

00:03:02.829 --> 00:03:04.299
zombie hand shirt before.

00:03:04.299 --> 00:03:08.389
One such flashback could be hinted at with
this scene of Richie at City Center.

00:03:08.389 --> 00:03:11.769
In the first one, this is where we learn that
Richie is afraid of clowns.

00:03:11.769 --> 00:03:15.489
This Paul Bunyan statue is shown, but doesn’t
do anything in the movie.

00:03:15.489 --> 00:03:19.349
In the book, Richie goes there by himself
one day and the statue comes to life and attacks

00:03:19.349 --> 00:03:22.760
him, so maybe that’s a scene we’ll get
to see in a flashback.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.150
There are other locations that they return
to from the first movie, like the hill leading

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:30.079
to the Barrens and this sewer pipe where they
first met Ben, it looks like the water is

00:03:30.079 --> 00:03:31.079
higher now.

00:03:31.079 --> 00:03:35.419
The town is once again littered with missing
child posters as it was in 1989, I found it

00:03:35.419 --> 00:03:39.109
interesting that it’s not the busy town
it once was, the streets are empty.

00:03:39.109 --> 00:03:43.260
It took me a while to decipher what this blurry
Daily Derry newspaper headline said, but I’ve

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.730
come to the conclusion that it says: “Body
found in Barrens”.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:51.230
This must be Dennis Torio, a boy who is murdered
in the novel and police find Georgie’s picture

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.530
at the crime scene.

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:56.170
Speaking of which, it looks like the ghost
of Georgie is not done haunting Bill.

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:59.430
This Chinese restaurant is called the Oriental
Jade, and this is where they meet up for the

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:00.939
first time in 27 years.

00:04:00.939 --> 00:04:04.370
I noticed that the gong in the background
here is moving, and I can just see Richie

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:08.219
slamming the gong to commence their meeting,
and disturbing all the other diners.

00:04:08.219 --> 00:04:12.239
OK, this shot shows thousands of balloons
under a bridge, one for every comment that

00:04:12.239 --> 00:04:13.650
tells me I look like Shaggy.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:17.900
No, but what this really is, is the event
that sets the new cycle of It into motion.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.989
It starts at a festival celebrating Derry.

00:04:19.989 --> 00:04:21.989
I’m guessing that’s what this is.

00:04:21.989 --> 00:04:25.889
Three drunk guys come to harass a gay couple
and one of them gets pushed off of a bridge

00:04:25.889 --> 00:04:29.540
where Pennywise is waiting, and bites the
guy’s arm off, before thousands of red,

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:32.669
“I love Derry” balloons rise up and hit
the bottom of the bridge.

00:04:32.669 --> 00:04:35.290
For this shot, I’m not going to go into
it because I don’t want some viewer to get

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:38.680
mad about spoilers and then some to my house
and bite my ear off or something, but if you

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:42.930
want a clue, I’ll just say to read Chapter
21 in the book, I think that’s what we’re

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:43.930
seeing here.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:47.199
I will however talk about this other shot
where we see the white clown gloves grabbing

00:04:47.199 --> 00:04:48.460
this little ball of light.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:52.220
When I talked about the first movie, I theorized
that these little lights that Beverly sees

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:56.460
down the throat of It are an interpretation
of the deadlights, the true form of It.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:00.850
And I think that’s what we’re seeing again
here, Pennywise using the deadlights to hypnotize

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:01.850
this girl.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:04.650
The little girl with the bruise on her face
can be seen wandering under the bleachers

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:06.580
during some kind of sporting event.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:10.880
My guess is that this is Dawn Roy, a 13 year
old girl found dead in McCairn Park.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:14.199
Mike tells everyone about the recent pattern
of dead or missing children at lunch at the

00:05:14.199 --> 00:05:17.199
Chinese restaurant and this is one of the
victims that he mentions.

00:05:17.199 --> 00:05:20.960
If you need a refresher on the Things You
Missed from the first movie, click the video

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:21.960
on the left.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.960
I’m planning a whole slate of videos about
It: Chapter 2 from now until the movie released

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:30.690
in September, so make sure you subscribe to
CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:34.210
that deathbell for notifications and I’ll
see you in the next one.

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:36.900
Assuming we allllll float.

